{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalCornerTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalCornerTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalBlockEquality","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRule"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_heckeIncl_mul_lastGen_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_heckeIncl_mul_lastGen_corner","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalCornerTrace.lean#L83-L106","doc":"**The block trace as a sum over corners.**  Splitting the diagonal sum by the cell carrying the\ntop entry replaces `SYT μ` by `Σ_{c corner} SYT (μ ∖ c)`; on each block the matrix is the downstairs\none and the Hoefsmit parameter is evaluated at `c(c) − c(r_S)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.axialDist_insertMax_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.axialDist_insertMax_top","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalCornerTrace.lean#L68-L81","doc":"**The last axial distance of a re-inserted tableau.**  `insertMax c S` carries `|μ|` at `c` and\n`|μ| − 1` wherever `S` carries it, so the distance between the two top cells is `c(c) − c(r_S)`.\nThis is where the corner `c` enters the arithmetic — as the *content* of the added cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.branchEquiv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.branchEquiv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalCornerTrace.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.branchEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.branchEquiv","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalCornerTrace.lean#L58-L63","doc":"**The branching rule as an equivalence.**  `SYTBranchingRule` proves `branchInv` injective and\nsurjective separately (it needed only the cardinality); the assembly needs the map itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.card_eraseCorner_of_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.card_eraseCorner_of_card","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalCornerTrace.lean#L53-L56","doc":"Removing a corner from a diagram of size `m + 2` leaves one of size `m + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}